ed to controversial R&B Singer/Producer [a14646] from 1994-1995 (annulled). At the time of passing, in a relationship with (and had reportedly planned to marry) Hip-hop mogul [a174951].\n\nUpon releasing her debut album \"[m=100995]\" in 1994, Aaliyah gained a steadily growing reputation for helping to redefine contemporary R&B, pop and hip hop, earning her the nicknames the \"Princess of R&B\" and \"Queen of Urban pop\".\nA sophomore album \"[m=101004]\" was released in 1996, and her final album, \"[m=35220]\", appeared earlier in the year of her tragic death.\nAaliyah's posthumous works range from 1 Movie and 2 singles: \"Poison featuring The Weeknd\" released in 2021 and \"Gone featuring Tank\" released in 2025.\n\nAaliyah has sold an estimated 24 to 32 million albums worldwide, alongside over 8 million certified sales in the United States.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:13733","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":4994648,"name":"Aaliyah Dana Haughton"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Aaaliyah","Aahliyah","Aailiyah","Aaleyah","Aalhyia","Aaliah","Aalijah","Aaliya","Aallayah","Aalyah","Aalyiah","Ah Lee Yah","Aliyaah","Aliyah","Aliyha","Alliya","Alliyah","Allyah","Alyah","アリーヤ","艾莉亞","艾莉雅","艾萊亞"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/13733-Aaliyah","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.aaliyah.com","http://www.facebook.com/AaliyahHaughton","http://www.instagram.com/aaliyah","http://twitter.com/Aaliyah","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaliyah","http://youtube.com/@aaliyahmusicvideo"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/37232/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"37232","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3IMcwcF3m3XZTV3ux2r8Jgku-ryWRjMuZT1refo43d4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:315/w:225/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3MjMy/LTEyNjQyNzQ1ODQu/anBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/KBfwbK7uwA2sbUr9RS_sb3DbClBCN0U_oWdZbxs3UV0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3MjMy/LTEyNjQyNzQ1ODQu/anBlZw.jp